---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/HeroSection.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Foundation Repair Cost in Tyler, TX | 2026 Pricing Guide"
  description="How much does foundation repair cost in Tyler, TX? Average prices range from $3,500–$15,000. See a full breakdown by repair type, pier count, and damage severity. Free inspection."
>
  <HeroSection
    h1="Foundation Repair Cost in Tyler, TX"
    subheading="Transparent pricing information for East Texas homeowners. Costs vary based on repair type, severity, and pier count — here's what to expect before you call."
    buttonText="Get a Free Estimate → (903) 582-7837"
  />

  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Average Foundation Repair Costs in Tyler, TX</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg mb-6">
        Foundation repair in Tyler typically costs between <strong>$3,500 and $15,000</strong> for a residential home. The wide range reflects differences in damage severity, the number of piers required, and the type of foundation. Here's a general breakdown:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-100">
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Repair Type</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Typical Cost Range</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Details</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 font-medium">Minor slab repair (2–4 piers)</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">$3,500 – $6,000</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">Localized settlement, 1–2 areas of concern</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50">
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 font-medium">Moderate slab repair (5–10 piers)</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">$6,000 – $10,000</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">Multiple zones settling, visible cracks throughout</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 font-medium">Major slab repair (10+ piers)</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">$10,000 – $20,000+</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">Whole-home settling, severe structural movement</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50">
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 font-medium">Pier &amp; beam repair</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">$1,500 – $8,000</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">Beam replacement, pier resetting, re-leveling</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 font-medium">Polyurethane foam injection</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">$800 – $3,000</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">Non-structural slabs: driveways, patios, garage floors</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50">
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3 font-medium">Foundation inspection</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">Free</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">No-cost through Tyler Foundation Pros</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
        These are estimates based on typical Tyler-area pricing as of 2026. Your actual cost will depend on your specific home and soil conditions. Call <a href="tel:9035827837" class="text-brand font-semibold hover:underline">(903) 582-7837</a> for a free written estimate with no obligation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What Determines the Cost?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">1. Number of Piers</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Steel push piers are the primary repair method for slab foundations in Tyler. Each pier costs roughly $800–$1,400 installed. A typical home repair uses 4–12 piers. The contractor determines how many are needed based on the size of your slab and the zones of settlement during the free inspection.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">2. Soil Conditions</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">East Texas clay soil varies in depth and reactivity across Smith County. In some areas, piers need to be driven 20–30 feet deep to reach stable load-bearing soil. Deeper piers require more materials and labor, which increases cost.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">3. Foundation Type</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Slab repairs typically cost more than pier-and-beam repairs because the work requires hydraulic lifting equipment and more piers. Pier-and-beam repairs involve crawl space access and beam/post work, which varies widely based on the age and condition of the existing structure.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">4. Accessibility</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">If your home has limited yard access, dense landscaping, or a deck built over part of the foundation, the repair becomes more complex. Contractors may need to remove and replace landscaping or other structures to access pier installation points.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">5. How Long You've Waited</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">This is the biggest cost factor most homeowners overlook. A repair that costs $5,000 with 4 piers today can become a $15,000 job with 12 piers in two years if the settlement continues unchecked. Early action almost always saves money.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Does Homeowner's Insurance Cover Foundation Repair in Texas?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        In most cases, <strong>no</strong>. Standard Texas homeowner's insurance policies exclude foundation damage caused by soil movement, settling, or shrinkage — which accounts for the vast majority of foundation problems in Tyler.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Insurance typically covers foundation damage only when it results from a sudden, covered peril — such as a plumbing leak under the slab or a flood event covered under a separate flood policy.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        If you believe your damage may be related to a covered event (like a burst pipe), document the cause carefully and file a claim. Your contractor can provide documentation of the damage. But for soil-related settling — the norm in East Texas — you should plan to pay out of pocket or finance the repair through your contractor.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Financing Options</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Many contractors in our network offer financing through third-party lenders, allowing you to spread the cost over 12–60 months. Common options include:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>0% APR promotional financing (12–18 months, credit-qualified)</li>
        <li>Low fixed-rate installment plans (36–60 months)</li>
        <li>Home equity lines of credit (for homeowners with available equity)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        Ask your contractor about financing during your free inspection. Approval decisions are typically made within minutes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Get an Accurate Estimate — Free</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Online cost guides can only give you a range. The only way to know exactly what your repair will cost is a free on-site inspection. A licensed contractor will:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>Assess your slab or pier-and-beam structure</li>
        <li>Identify the specific zones of settlement</li>
        <li>Determine how many piers or what repair method is needed</li>
        <li>Give you a written estimate with line-item pricing</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        No charge. No sales pressure. Just an honest assessment. Call <a href="tel:9035827837" class="text-brand font-semibold hover:underline">(903) 582-7837</a> to schedule yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    heading="Get Your Free Foundation Estimate in Tyler"
    subtext="A licensed Tyler-area contractor will inspect your foundation and give you a written estimate at no charge. Typically scheduled within 48 hours."
    buttonText="Call (903) 582-7837 — Free Estimate"
  />
</Layout>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does foundation repair cost in Tyler, TX?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Foundation repair in Tyler typically costs between $3,500 and $15,000 for a residential home. Minor repairs with 2–4 piers run $3,500–$6,000. Moderate repairs with 5–10 piers run $6,000–$10,000. Major repairs with 10+ piers can exceed $15,000–$20,000."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does homeowner's insurance cover foundation repair in Texas?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "In most cases, no. Standard Texas homeowner's insurance excludes foundation damage caused by soil movement or settling. Coverage may apply if damage is caused by a sudden event like a burst pipe, but soil-related settling — the most common cause in Tyler — is typically not covered."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does each foundation pier cost in Tyler?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Each steel push pier in Tyler typically costs $800–$1,400 installed, depending on depth required and soil conditions. Most homes need between 4 and 12 piers for a full repair."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
